WEBVTT

00:01.430 --> 00:04.530
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:04.530 --> 00:08.170
My thoughts travel the wilderness

00:08.170 --> 00:16.100
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

00:21.250 --> 00:27.760
Under the scorching rays of the sun,
what thoughts cross your mind?

00:27.760 --> 00:33.700
What does your grief-stricken gaze reflect now?

00:33.700 --> 00:42.640
If I can keep from losing my way,
step by step, it should be easy

00:42.640 --> 00:47.410
Like the wind

00:47.410 --> 00:50.480
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:50.480 --> 00:54.080
I travel the dawn-lit wilderness

00:54.080 --> 01:00.520
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

01:00.520 --> 01:07.330
Don't be afraid, change is
nothing to be frightened of

01:07.330 --> 01:13.440
As long as you are yourself, I will be with you

01:13.440 --> 01:20.180
Dreaming of tranquil days

01:20.180 --> 01:27.410
The roadless journey continues

01:37.230 --> 01:40.560
How long ago will it have been now?

01:40.560 --> 01:44.700
There is no one who is able to say for certain.

01:44.700 --> 01:48.570
When civilizations were first
coming into being on this planet,

01:48.570 --> 01:53.640
the world had a need for our powers.

01:53.640 --> 01:56.510
However...

01:56.510 --> 01:58.710
As time passed,

01:58.710 --> 02:03.780
we came to be ostracized and persecuted.

02:05.650 --> 02:09.460
Thus, in order to keep from
repeating this unfortunate history,

02:09.460 --> 02:11.630
we decided to hide the entirety of our existence

02:11.630 --> 02:16.220
in the depths of the shadows of legend.

02:18.870 --> 02:26.340
There can be no exception,
even for a being made by man.

02:26.340 --> 02:29.740
With Project Leviathan now suspended,

02:29.740 --> 02:34.810
there are no longer any
benefits to leaving Ellis at large.

02:37.350 --> 02:42.760
To say nothing of allowing
her to set foot in that place.

02:42.760 --> 02:44.660
It is out of the question.

02:46.930 --> 02:50.600
If legend becomes no longer legend,

02:50.600 --> 02:54.940
it will place all of our people in danger.

02:54.940 --> 02:59.810
I'm sure you remember the incident
from 10 years ago as well as I do.

02:59.810 --> 03:03.380
We do not have time to be acting deliberately.

03:03.380 --> 03:08.520
I instruct you once again.
Capture Ellis immediately.

03:08.520 --> 03:11.210
That is the collective will of our people.

03:17.530 --> 03:21.520
And I am just another one of the people.

03:41.280 --> 03:43.880
As tasteless as ever, I see.

03:48.290 --> 03:50.290
- Oh.
- Huh?

03:50.290 --> 03:51.850
That.

04:15.880 --> 04:18.450
So it suddenly stopped.

04:18.450 --> 04:22.890
Well, the car definitely looks like
it could break down at any second.

05:00.800 --> 05:04.770
Yeah, this is no good.

05:04.770 --> 05:07.640
It's going to be tomorrow
morning at the earliest.

05:07.640 --> 05:09.540
I'll call you when I'm done.

05:09.540 --> 05:12.370
- Where can I reach you?
- I haven't decided yet.

05:12.370 --> 05:15.480
Oh, you were traveling in this thing?

05:15.480 --> 05:17.680
Then I'll refer you to a hotel.

05:17.680 --> 05:19.850
Oh, in that case, could you refer me, too?

05:19.850 --> 05:21.080
Huh?

05:21.080 --> 05:23.650
You guys are... husband and wife, right?

05:23.650 --> 05:25.310
What?!

05:28.560 --> 05:32.030
You seem to be far apart in age, but...

05:32.030 --> 05:35.660
How do I say this? You guys have
the same exact feel about you.

05:35.660 --> 05:39.530
- Was I wrong?
- Listen, now! We're...

05:40.940 --> 05:44.430
Mister, show a little compassion.

05:52.980 --> 05:54.450
I see.

05:54.450 --> 05:57.980
Then I'll ask them to give you separate rooms.

06:01.490 --> 06:05.660
Honestly! What a thing to say!

06:05.660 --> 06:07.530
It can't be helped, right?

06:07.530 --> 06:09.700
Explaining how we're related would be...

06:09.700 --> 06:12.670
I know! But...

06:12.670 --> 06:15.100
Of all things, husband and wife is just...

06:17.040 --> 06:20.580
Hey, hold on, you guys!

06:20.580 --> 06:22.980
Tickets to a special dinner.

06:22.980 --> 06:25.450
It's the top restaurant in town.

06:25.450 --> 06:27.150
What? Are you sure?

06:27.150 --> 06:34.020
Unfortunately, I had to bury
my wife three years ago, so...

06:34.020 --> 06:35.720
Thank you.

06:35.720 --> 06:38.930
Your wife looks like the simple sort.

06:38.930 --> 06:42.800
Take her out for a nice meal
and she'll cheer right up.

06:42.800 --> 06:45.630
Right...

06:45.630 --> 06:47.530
Good luck!

07:08.790 --> 07:11.730
Wow, it's a nice room.

07:11.730 --> 07:13.560
We'll come for you later.

07:13.560 --> 07:15.150
We'll be waiting.

07:17.470 --> 07:19.870
Now, I guess I'll take a shower.

07:19.870 --> 07:22.000
We're going to go eat with them?

07:22.000 --> 07:23.600
Huh?

07:23.600 --> 07:25.740
It'll save us the cost of a meal, and besides...

07:25.740 --> 07:27.830
Because you're husband and wife?

07:30.080 --> 07:32.080
That's not it.

07:32.080 --> 07:34.950
You want to eat out at a nice
place once in a while, you know?

07:34.950 --> 07:36.680
That's why you're showering?

07:36.680 --> 07:38.690
It doesn't matter, you're showering, too.

07:38.690 --> 07:40.620
You're coming with me, aren't you?

07:41.820 --> 07:43.690
Yessir.

07:48.160 --> 07:51.860
Uh, the shower, we can do separately...

08:19.630 --> 08:24.100
Hey, there are only two seats here...

08:24.100 --> 08:25.970
Your companions will be seated over there.

08:25.970 --> 08:27.760
We'll show you the way.

09:11.250 --> 09:15.080
Doug, I got a hold of some
nice wine. Let's have some.

09:15.080 --> 09:16.850
Really?

09:25.190 --> 09:29.260
- A decanter?
- You see, wines...

09:29.260 --> 09:35.930
...open up to their true potential when
they're exposed to the air outside.

09:38.310 --> 09:40.780
Yes...

09:40.780 --> 09:42.740
Just like humans.

09:54.690 --> 09:56.590
Beautiful, isn't it?

10:00.330 --> 10:03.730
Why don't you at least say,
"Yeah, you're right"?

10:03.730 --> 10:05.260
Why?

10:47.240 --> 10:49.180
Nadie...

11:02.990 --> 11:04.920
Nadie...

11:24.110 --> 11:26.210
I love you.

11:26.210 --> 11:28.820
I'm not letting go of you tonight.

11:28.820 --> 11:30.680
Neither am I.

11:41.860 --> 11:44.170
Wiñay Marka.

11:44.170 --> 11:46.830
Do you have an idea of where it is?

11:46.830 --> 11:48.340
Nope.

11:48.340 --> 11:50.770
But we do have a guide.

11:50.770 --> 11:53.440
Even though he's a weird guy.

11:53.440 --> 11:55.180
You be careful.

11:55.180 --> 11:58.270
Thank you. Nice to know you worry about us.

12:02.480 --> 12:05.990
But I need to look after that child.

12:05.990 --> 12:09.090
I'm sure she'll manage fine
on her own without you.

12:09.090 --> 12:10.960
It'll be fine.

12:21.100 --> 12:22.500
The lights!

12:54.970 --> 12:57.370
Ellis?

12:57.370 --> 12:59.930
- Ellis?!
- Here.

13:03.840 --> 13:06.510
I sincerely apologize for the disturbance.

13:06.510 --> 13:09.920
Please carry on and enjoy your meal.

13:19.130 --> 13:20.920
Nadie...

13:33.340 --> 13:35.310
Ellis...

13:35.310 --> 13:37.300
Taking a detour, are we?

13:39.250 --> 13:42.310
Delicious! That's the top
restaurant in town for you!

13:45.990 --> 13:48.220
Oh, we have to pay separately for the alcohol.

13:48.220 --> 13:49.920
Careful not to drink too much.

13:49.920 --> 13:51.990
I'll pay for what I drink.

13:51.990 --> 13:54.560
Oh, really. Then that's fine.

13:54.560 --> 13:57.970
What do you plan to do
when you run out of money?

13:57.970 --> 14:00.940
Hmm... what will I do?

14:00.940 --> 14:02.870
Bounty hunting?

14:06.610 --> 14:10.910
No, I'll think of some other way.

14:10.910 --> 14:12.850
Ellis doesn't want me doing that anyway.

14:12.850 --> 14:15.450
I see. Then that's fine.

14:15.450 --> 14:20.450
What's this? You don't like
me being a bounty hunter?

14:20.450 --> 14:22.190
Because I'm a woman?

14:22.190 --> 14:25.530
Relying on a gun is no way to live.

14:25.530 --> 14:28.230
You're a bounty hunter yourself.

14:28.230 --> 14:31.560
I just didn't know any
other way to make a living.

14:34.130 --> 14:38.340
What you need to make a life aren't guns.

14:38.340 --> 14:41.000
I realized that too late.

14:47.310 --> 14:50.380
What kind of grandpa talk is that?

14:50.380 --> 14:53.050
You're still young, too.

14:53.050 --> 14:56.250
After all, you were mistaken for my husband.

15:00.930 --> 15:03.430
Ignore me, will you?

15:03.430 --> 15:05.470
Again?

15:05.470 --> 15:09.030
I am so very sorry! Please wait one moment.

15:13.970 --> 15:15.570
Ellis.

15:17.380 --> 15:19.440
She won't come for me...

15:33.230 --> 15:35.400
Ricardo's actions are a problem.

15:35.400 --> 15:39.530
The key is to keep him
from getting close to Ellis.

15:39.530 --> 15:42.570
There must be ways to do that.

15:42.570 --> 15:44.970
- Go back.
- Yes, ma'am.

15:50.240 --> 15:53.150
Is there something you want to say to me?

15:53.150 --> 15:54.610
No.

15:57.550 --> 16:01.990
Have you ever seen a witch's powers at work?

16:01.990 --> 16:04.960
If you mean the power Ellis invoked...

16:04.960 --> 16:08.160
That was nothing compared
to a real witch's powers.

16:08.160 --> 16:10.220
It's bound to be more spectacular.

16:13.000 --> 16:14.340
Surely...

16:14.340 --> 16:17.970
I wonder if they're having electrical problems.

16:17.970 --> 16:19.670
Pardon me.

16:24.140 --> 16:26.580
Wanna go sit with Mommy and Daddy?

16:41.200 --> 16:44.650
What's going on? Why just bring Lirio over now?

16:55.610 --> 16:57.600
- Nadie!
- Huh?

17:03.650 --> 17:05.310
Ellis!

17:09.360 --> 17:11.150
Gracias.

17:18.030 --> 17:20.090
Hey, there. Sorry. Sorry.

17:35.620 --> 17:37.280
Ellis!

17:45.130 --> 17:48.660
Once we deliver this girl
to the designated location,

17:48.660 --> 17:52.600
our mission will be over.

17:52.600 --> 17:54.590
That was disappointingly easy.

18:01.140 --> 18:05.210
Oh... Ellis...

18:05.210 --> 18:07.410
- Take the side road.
- Yes, ma'am!

18:11.550 --> 18:13.210
Ellis...

18:18.490 --> 18:20.260
He's not coming after us?

18:29.440 --> 18:32.170
- Why isn't he?
- Here they come!

18:37.710 --> 18:40.380
Nadie!

18:40.380 --> 18:42.550
Give Ellis back!

18:42.550 --> 18:45.280
- I refuse!
- Blue-eyes!

18:47.220 --> 18:48.860
Nadie, don't interfere!

18:48.860 --> 18:51.760
Get out of here, you double-crosser!

18:51.760 --> 18:54.630
Ellis, are you okay?!

18:54.630 --> 18:56.230
Ellis!

18:56.230 --> 18:57.700
Nadie!

19:24.630 --> 19:26.290
Ellis!

19:54.390 --> 19:56.620
Are you okay?

19:56.620 --> 19:58.260
You came for me.

19:58.260 --> 20:00.820
You dummy. Of course I did.

20:13.810 --> 20:15.670
They got us.

20:24.590 --> 20:27.350
Ellis...

20:27.350 --> 20:30.360
I-I was just asked to do that...

20:30.360 --> 20:32.990
I was told to say the repairs
were going to take time

20:32.990 --> 20:35.960
t-to keep you here in town...

20:35.960 --> 20:41.270
You were told to hand us those
restaurant tickets, too, right?

20:41.270 --> 20:42.860
Yeah...

20:44.270 --> 20:46.010
A-All right.

20:46.010 --> 20:49.640
I won't charge you for the repairs,
so we should be good, right?

20:56.520 --> 20:58.390
Wh-What is it? What's wrong?

20:58.390 --> 20:59.880
Hey, Ellis...

21:06.960 --> 21:08.860
Wh-What?

21:08.860 --> 21:11.770
- Do we look like husband and wife?
- Huh?

21:11.770 --> 21:13.500
A happy couple.

21:13.500 --> 21:16.740
Husband and wife are man and woman.

21:16.740 --> 21:18.010
It doesn't matter.

21:18.010 --> 21:21.770
Um... This makes it hard for me to drive...

21:24.010 --> 21:26.040
Well, I guess that's okay.

21:38.790 --> 21:40.730
Don't...

21:40.730 --> 21:42.890
...stick so close together.

21:51.040 --> 21:54.780
Hey... Could it be that...

21:54.780 --> 21:58.910
...you're acting like this because
Ricardo and I were being friendly?

21:58.910 --> 22:00.680
That's not it.

22:02.080 --> 22:03.780
That's not it, right?

22:03.780 --> 22:06.310
Okay, let's go.

22:13.060 --> 22:15.320
Teehee.

22:23.040 --> 22:27.440
Ellis, the artificial witch,
has no capacity for emotions.

22:27.440 --> 22:30.410
That report is already...

22:30.410 --> 22:32.570
...a thing of the past.

22:36.550 --> 22:40.350
Like a neverending summer

22:40.350 --> 22:43.790
Like flowers that never die

22:43.790 --> 22:47.690
Those arms you've wrapped around me

22:47.690 --> 22:55.830
Don't ever let go of me

23:02.040 --> 23:05.650
Even if I try clinging to you

23:05.650 --> 23:11.450
My heart still heeds a different evanescence

23:11.450 --> 23:15.420
Counting the rhythm of time by it

23:15.420 --> 23:19.530
A night of red stars

23:19.530 --> 23:23.530
The vanishing warmth

23:23.530 --> 23:27.470
I want to keep it here

23:27.470 --> 23:33.870
You, with your eyes closed

23:33.870 --> 23:37.840
Yearning over and over

23:37.840 --> 23:41.180
Even if I can't go anywhere

23:41.180 --> 23:45.420
When the heartache comes to a stop

23:45.420 --> 23:51.730
To the two of us, this moment is...

23:51.730 --> 23:56.720
...everything
